.TH on_shutdown 3 2026-11-20 DarqOS "DarqOS Library Manual"
.SH NAME
on_shutdown \- finish a program at shutdown
.SH LIBRARY
.I darq
.SH SYNOPSIS
.BI on_shutdown( handler ", " loop )
.PP
.BI handler( reboot ", " now ) " -> ShutdownLater | None"
.PP
class \fIShutdownLater\fP:
    def note(\fItext\fP)
    def done()
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR on_shutdown ()
has
.I handler
called, on
.IR loop ,
the program's own event loop, when the system shuts down, or reboots
.RI ( reboot ),
so the program can finish what it must first: save, or ask the
operator.
.PP
The handler returns None when it's finished, and the program ends.
Or it returns a
.BR ShutdownLater ,
and calls its
.BR done ()
when it's finished, from any thread;
.BR note ()
says what it's doing meanwhile, which
.BR pyloader (8)
tells the p-kernel, with WAIT, every 4 seconds, and the Terminal shows.
If it's silent, or takes longer than 60 seconds, it's called again, with
.I now
true: it should save what it can, at once, and return, and the program
ends; it's killed 3 seconds later otherwise.
.PP
Without a handler, a program ends at once at shutdown.
.SH ERRORS
None.
.SH HISTORY
Introduced in \fISecond Edition\fP.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
def finish(reboot, now):
    if now or not unsaved:
        return None
    later = darq.ShutdownLater("saving")
    save(then=later.done)
    return later

darq.on_shutdown(finish, loop)
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR on_shutdown (3),
.BR shutdown_now (2),
.BR shutdown_state (2),
.BR pkernel (8),
.BR pyloader (8)
